lina: Heads-up: getting sporadic "Unexpected end of JSON input" in the Node SDK when consuming SSE. Repro in our onboarding sample with node 18 + sdk-js v0.6.4. Seems to spike when users close the tab mid-stream or when the runtime rotates auth. Anyone seen this pattern?

sam: yep. We hit this in staging last week. The current node reader naively does JSON.parse per 'data:' event and fails if an event is split across TCP chunks.

vikas: can you share minimal repro and the raw bytes? We need a deterministic test. /cc @tori for runtime auth rotate behavior.

lina: minimal repro attached inline:```js
// naive handler that breaks
res.on('data', chunk => {
  const s = chunk.toString();
  const events = s.split('\n\n');
  events.forEach(e => {
    if (e.startsWith('data: ')) {
      const obj = JSON.parse(e.slice(6)); // throws when split mid-json
      onEvent(obj);"
    }
  });
});
```
error: `SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input`

tori: runtime note: when we do an auth rotate or refresh we may close the socket and open a fresh connection. We don't currently emit a pre-rotate control event, so any partial bytes in transit are lost. Client MUST treat SSE as a byte stream and reassemble before parsing.

sam: two orthogonal fixes: 1) server emits control events with seq/resume tokens, 2) SDK keeps a persistent trailing buffer across reconnects and only parse once you see the SSE delimiter (`\n\n`). Node SDK currently doesn't persist the tail buffer across reconnects.

vikas: I'll add a fix in node SDK: maintain a persistent tail buffer across reconnect attempts, split on the full delimiter, and only JSON.parse once a whole event is present. Also plan unit tests that simulate: mid-event client close, auth rotate, and proxy re-chunking.

lina: small robust parse snippet for sample apps (to add to onboarding):```js
let tail = '';
res.on('data', chunk => {
  tail += chunk.toString();
  let sepIdx;
  while ((sepIdx = tail.indexOf('\n\n')) !== -1) {
    const raw = tail.slice(0, sepIdx);
    tail = tail.slice(sepIdx + 2);
    if (!raw) continue;
    if (raw.startsWith('data: ')) {
      try {
        const obj = JSON.parse(raw.slice(6));
        handle(obj);
      } catch (err) {
        // if parse fails here, log and stash raw to retry after reconnect
        console.warn('sse parse failed, keeping tail for retry');
        tail = raw + '\n\n' + tail; // requeue
        break;
      }
    }
  }
});
// preserve `tail` across reconnects and prepend it to the next stream's incoming data
```

tori: Agree. On runtime side we'll add an optional pre-rotate control event when we can:
```
event: control
data: {"type":"pre_rotate","last_seq": 789}

```
and on the new connection we can emit a resume control event echoing last_seq. If rotate is forced (401 mid-stream) we'll try to include a resume token on the new stream so clients can detect gaps.

vikas: I'll also add an opt-in strict-seq mode: if server provides `seq` in each data payload, SDK can assert contiguous seqs and surface `sse_resume_gap` telemetry when gaps detected.

ci-bot: Created issue #4420: "sdk-js(node): SSE partial-chunk parse errors during client disconnect/auth rotate - tail buffer + seq handling" assigned to vikas.

lina: I'll update sample-app README + onboarding notes with the robust snippet and a troubleshooting FAQ entry. Also call out increasing token TTL as a short-term mitigation for long-lived streams.

vikas: Plan summary: 1) sticky tail buffer across reconnects, 2) added tests for abort/rechunk/rotate, 3) add telemetry counters `sse_parse_error` and `sse_resume_gap`, 4) document workaround and sample code. ETA: PR tomorrow.

tori: runtime will open PR for pre-rotate/resume events and we'll sync on exact JSON shape.

lina: great—assigning follow-ups: vikas (sdk patch + tests + telemetry), tori (runtime pre-rotate PR), me (docs/sample-app). Will smoke test when PRs land. :thumbsup:
